{#
  Methods of the atac-seq workflow (snakemake-methods). Only the steps of this
  configuration are described; every value comes from config, the params of
  the methods rule (workflow/rules/methods.smk) or workflow/scripts/methods.py.
  tool() cites a tool with its version at its first mention, in render order
  (macros count where they are called; call them with | trim). Prose lines
  of a paragraph are joined; keep {% if %} blocks on their own lines, and
  don't start a line with "|", "- " or "1. " (they would be kept as table rows
  or list items).
#}
{% set blacklist = reference["blacklist"] %}
{% set tss = reference["tss"] %}
{% set macs2 = config["macs2"] %}
{% set tagalign_text = "Tn5-shifted tagAlign files (+4 bp on the plus strand, −5 bp on the minus strand)" %}
{% macro blacklist_text() %}
{% if blacklist["source"] == "encode" %}
the ENCODE blacklist {{ blacklist["accession"] }} {{ cite("amemiya2019") }}
{% if "lifted_from" in blacklist %}
, lifted over from {{ blacklist["lifted_from"] }} with
{{ tool("liftover", code("-minMatch=0.5")) }},
{% endif %}
{% else %}
the blacklist {{ cite("amemiya2019") }} from {{ tool("annotationhub") }}
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
{% macro chipseeker_text() %}
{{ tool("chipseeker", "TSS region ± " ~ number(tss_region) ~ " bp") }}, using a
TxDb built from the Ensembl GTF with {{ tool("txdbmaker") }} and
{{ tool("rtracklayer") }}
{% endmacro %}
{% macro macs2_text(gsize) %}
Peaks were called with
{{ tool("macs2", code(macs2_options) ~ ", effective genome size " ~ gsize) }},
keeping the {{ number(macs2["cap_num_peak"]) }} peaks with the lowest
p-values. Peaks overlapping {{ blacklist_text() | trim }} or on chromosomes not
matching {{ code(keep_chr) }} were removed with {{ tool("bedtools") }}.
{% endmacro %}
{% macro tss_text() %}
{% if tss["source"] == "encode" %}
TSSs of ENCODE file {{ tss["accession"] }}
{% if "lifted_from" in tss %}
, lifted over from {{ tss["lifted_from"] }} with {{ tool("liftover") }}
{% endif %}
{% else %}
5' ends of protein-coding genes of the Ensembl GTF
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
{% macro deseq2_sentences(features) %}
With {{ tool("deseq2") }}, sample PCA (the {{ number(pca_ntop) }} most variable
{{ features }}) and Pearson correlations used variance-stabilised counts (blind
to the conditions).
{% if contrasts %}
{{ features | capitalize }} with < {{ min_count }} insertions in all samples
together were removed, and differential accessibility ({{ contrast_text }}) was
tested (design {{ code("~ condition") }}; Wald test of {{ lfc_text }};
Benjamini–Hochberg adjusted p < {{ fdr }}, {{ citation("benjamini1995") }});
log2 fold changes were shrunken with {{ tool("ashr") }} for ranking and plots.
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
Paired-end ATAC-seq data of {{ n_samples }} samples ({{ samples_text }}) were
analysed with the atac-seq workflow {{ workflow_version }}
(https://github.com/niekwit/atac-seq) in {{ tool("snakemake") }}
{% if not te_only %}
, following the ENCODE ATAC-seq pipeline v2.2.3 {{ cite("encode2020") }} unless
stated otherwise
{% endif %}
. The {{ genome_name }} and gene annotation were from Ensembl release
{{ reference["release"] }} {{ cite("dyer2025") }}.

## Read processing{{ "" if te_only else " and alignment" }}

Read quality was assessed with {{ tool("fastqc") }}. Adapters were trimmed with
{{ tool("cutadapt", code(cutadapt_options)) }}.
{% if not te_only %}
Read pairs were aligned with {{ tool("bowtie2", code(bowtie2_options)) }}.
{% if multimapping %}
Reads with more than {{ multimapping }} alignments were removed and the others
were assigned one of their alignments at random (ENCODE assign_multimappers);
{% else %}
Reads with a mapping quality below {{ mapq_thresh }} were removed;
{% endif %}
only properly paired primary alignments were kept, with {{ tool("samtools") }}
via {{ tool("pysam") }}. Duplicates were marked with {{ tool("picard") }}
MarkDuplicates and removed, together with alignments on
{{ filter_chrs | join_and }} ({{ code("samtools view -F 1804 -f 2") }}).
{% endif %}

{% if not te_only %}
## Peak calling

Alignments were converted to {{ tagalign_text }}
{% if config["subsample_reads"] %}
and subsampled to {{ number(config["subsample_reads"]) }} reads
{% endif %}
. Each replicate was split into two pseudoreplicates ({{ seed_text }}), and the
replicates and pseudoreplicates of each condition were pooled.
{{ macs2_text(code(macs2["gsize"])) | trim }}
Reproducible peaks of each condition were selected by naive overlap (pooled
peaks overlapping a peak of both replicates or pseudoreplicates by ≥ 50%)
{% if idr %}
and by
{{ tool("idr", "IDR < " ~ config["idr"]["threshold"] ~ ", peaks ranked by p-value") }}
{% endif %}
, and optimal and conservative peak sets were chosen from the comparisons of
true replicates and pseudoreplicates as in ENCODE.
{% if replicated %}
In addition, pooled peaks reproducible in
{% if all_replicates %}
all the replicates of a condition
{% else %}
at least {{ min_fraction }} of the replicates of a condition (rounded up, at
least 2)
{% endif %}
were reported (overlap ≥ {{ min_overlap }}
{% if idr %}
, or IDR below the threshold for all pairs
{% endif %}
).
{% endif %}
Fold-enrichment and p-value signal tracks were generated with MACS2 bdgcmp and
{{ tool("ucsc_bigwig") }}. Optimal peaks were annotated with
{{ chipseeker_text() | trim }}.

{% set regions_text = "ENCODE DNase I hypersensitive sites, promoters, enhancers and the blacklist"
  if reference["annotation_regions"] else "the blacklist" %}
## Quality control

QC metrics were calculated as in ENCODE: library complexity (NRF, PBC1 and
PBC2, without mitochondrial reads), fraction of mitochondrial reads
({{ config["mito_chr_name"] }}), TSS enrichment ({{ tss_text() | trim }}), fragment
length distribution and GC bias (Picard CollectInsertSizeMetrics and
CollectGcBiasMetrics), fraction of reads in {{ regions_text }}, fraction of
reads in peaks, and fingerprints and Jensen–Shannon distances of the
replicates with
{{ tool("deeptools", "plotFingerprint, MAPQ ≥ " ~ mapq_thresh) }}. Further QC
was done with {{ tool("ataqv") }}, and reports were combined with
{{ tool("multiqc") }}.
{% endif %}

{% if deseq2 and not te_only %}
## Differential accessibility

The optimal peak sets ({{ peak_method }}) of all conditions were merged into
consensus peaks (BEDTools merge). Tn5 insertions (5' read ends) per peak were
counted with {{ tool("featurecounts", code(count_options)) }}.
{{ deseq2_sentences("peaks") | trim }}
Consensus peaks were annotated with ChIPseeker as above.
{% endif %}

{% if te %}
{% set te_config = config.get("te", {}) %}
{% set classes = te_config.get("classes") or [] %}
## Transposable elements

Trimmed read pairs were aligned again with
{{ tool("bowtie2", code("--seed 42 " ~ config["bowtie2"]["extra"])) }} in
default mode, which reports one of the best alignments of multimapping reads at
random. Properly paired alignments were kept, and duplicates (same fragment
coordinates and strand) and alignments on {{ filter_chrs | join_and }} were
removed with {{ tool("pysam") }} and {{ tool("samtools") }}. Read pairs were
classed as multimapping when a mate had an equally good alternative alignment
(XS ≥ AS) and MAPQ < 2. The RepeatMasker annotation {{ cite("smit2015") }} of
{{ reference["ucsc_genome"] }} was downloaded from the UCSC Genome Browser
{{ cite("kent2002") }}, and
{% if classes %}
repeats of the classes {{ classes | join_and }}
{% else %}
all repeats
{% endif %}
were used. Tn5 insertions in repeats were counted with
{{ tool("featurecounts", code(count_options) ~ "; with " ~ code("-M")
  ~ " for all read pairs, without for uniquely mapping read pairs") }}
and summed per subfamily, family and class, with counts per million insertions
and log2 enrichment (fraction of insertions over fraction of the genome
covered, pseudocount 1). CPM-normalised insertion tracks were made with
{{ tool("deeptools", "bamCoverage " ~ code("--binSize " ~ bin_size
  ~ " --normalizeUsing CPM --Offset 1")) }}
and averaged per condition (bigwigAverage).
{% if profile["subfamilies"] %}
Insertion profiles over full-length copies (covering ≥
{{ percent(profile["min_consensus_fraction"]) }} of the consensus) of selected
subfamilies were calculated with computeMatrix scale-regions (body
{{ number(profile["body_length"]) }} bp, flanks {{ number(profile["flank"]) }}
bp, 50 bp bins) and plotted with plotProfile.
{% endif %}

{% if deseq2 %}
{% set normalisation_text = "median-of-ratios size factors over the subfamilies"
  if te_config.get("normalisation", "deseq2") == "deseq2"
  else "size factors proportional to all kept insertions of a sample" %}
{% if te_only %}
Subfamily counts (all read pairs) were normalised with
{{ normalisation_text }}. {{ deseq2_sentences("subfamilies") | trim }}
{% else %}
Subfamily counts (all read pairs; {{ normalisation_text }}) were analysed with
DESeq2 as the consensus peaks.
{% endif %}
{% if contrasts %}
Heatmaps show row z-scores of variance-stabilised counts of
{% if "all" in heatmap["subfamilies"] %}
the significant subfamilies (at most {{ heatmap["max_per_class"] }} per class)
{% else %}
selected subfamilies
{% endif %}
of
{% if "all" in heatmap["classes"] %}
all classes
{% else %}
the classes {{ heatmap["classes"] | join_and }}
{% endif %}
.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% set gsize_text = "the total chromosome length" %}
{% if te_only %}
For peak calling, these alignments were converted to {{ tagalign_text }} and
pooled per condition. {{ macs2_text(gsize_text) | trim }}
{% else %}
Peaks were called from these alignments as above (MACS2 with
{{ gsize_text }} as effective genome size, blacklist filtering).
{% endif %}
{% if all_replicates %}
